-- title:
--   Ordinarity forces the unit component to be of multiplicative type
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$. Let $B$ be a commutative ring carrying a Hopf algebra structure over $\mathbb{Z}/p$ whose comultiplication is cocommutative and which is finite as a $\mathbb{Z}/p$-module, and let $B^c$, $B^e$ likewise be commutative rings with finite $\mathbb{Z}/p$-Hopf algebra structures. Suppose given bialgebra maps $q^c : B \to B^c$, $\pi^e : B \to B^e$, $\sigma : B^e \to B$ and $\Theta : B \to B^c \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}/p} B^e$ such that: $q^c$ and $\pi^e$ are surjective; the kernel of $\pi^e$ as an algebra map is the nilradical of $B$; $\pi^e \circ \sigma$ is the identity of $B^e$; $B^e$ is formally unramified over $\mathbb{Z}/p$; the kernel of $q^c$ is the ideal generated by the image under $\sigma$ of the augmentation ideal, i.e. the kernel of the counit algebra map of $B^e$; $\Theta$ is $b \mapsto (q^c \otimes \pi^e)(\Delta b)$; and $B^c$ is a local ring. Assume moreover an ordinarity hypothesis: there exist a commutative ring $M$ with a $\mathbb{Z}/p$-Hopf algebra structure that is finite and free as a $\mathbb{Z}/p$-module, a commutative ring $E$ with a $\mathbb{Z}/p$-Hopf algebra structure, and a bijective bialgebra map $B \to M \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}/p} E$, with $E$ reduced and the Cartier dual of $M$ reduced. Then the Cartier dual of $B^c$ — the $\mathbb{Z}/p$-linear dual `Module.Dual (ZMod p) Bc` with its Cartier-dual ring structure — is reduced.
--
--   In the language of group schemes this says that the connected component of the identity of an ordinary finite commutative group scheme over $\mathbb{F}_p$ is of multiplicative type, the connected–étale splitting data for $B$ being carried here as explicit hypotheses on $q^c$, $\pi^e$, $\sigma$ and $\Theta$. It feeds the analysis of $p$-divisible groups of level one over $\mathbb{Z}/p$, being used by [`PDivisibleGroup.forall_exists_bijective_tensorProduct_isReduced_cartierDual_of_level_one_zmodp`](thm.html#PDivisibleGroup.forall_exists_bijective_tensorProduct_isReduced_cartierDual_of_level_one_zmodp).
